PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority view (cols 1-5,8,9) strongly favors C: Ontario ESA (Oct 2021 amendments via Bill 27/Working for Workers Act) voids new non-competes for provincially regulated employees except true C-suite execs or sale-of-business; none of A/B/D/E qualify and all are provincial. Schedule 1 banks are federally regulated (Bank Act), so ESA ban inapplicable; Canada Labour Code + common-law reasonableness govern instead. Thus only C can still include a potentially valid clause in a 2023 agreement. 

Minority counters: Col 6 argues E (2019 hire) is grandfathered pre-ban so enforceable if reasonable at common law. Cols 7/10 argue B (associate lawyer) may have fiduciary/professional carve-outs under Law Society rules or precedent despite 2022 start. 

Key unresolved tension: whether ESA "voids" language applies only to post-2021 inclusions or reaches ongoing agreements, and whether any regulated-profession exceptions exist beyond the statutory text. Dates of hire noted but jurisdiction (federal vs provincial) appears decisive per detailed responses. No corrections to facts yet; C consensus appears robust.}

